# mp-754090 (Li4Fe2TeWO12) validation system, EFFECTIVE nearest-neighbor parameterization,
# DFT-derived J with PLACEHOLDER DMI. First-pass qualitative check only -- see below.
#
# Only the magnetic Fe sublattice is modeled (framework Li/Te/W/O sites carry no spin and
# are dropped from the geometry entirely), same convention as in.pdfeir_effective.lammps.
#
# --- J derivation (real DFT, see outputs/dft_ordering_validation.csv, mp-754090) ---
#   E_FM  = -125.85042289 eV (0_fm, MAGMOM Fe = +5,+5)
#   E_AFM = -125.80218935 eV (1_afm, MAGMOM Fe = -5,+5)
#   dE = E_AFM - E_FM = 0.04823354 eV per formula-unit cell (2 Fe atoms: Fe0, Fe1)
#   Fe-Fe distances (computed from POSCAR + periodic images, see scratchpad): the AFM flip
#   here inverts Fe0 only, so ONLY Fe0-Fe1 (opposite-sublattice) bonds change sign; Fe0-Fe0
#   and Fe1-Fe1 (same-sublattice) bonds stay aligned in both FM and AFM. The nearest
#   opposite-sublattice shell has z=4 neighbors, tightly clustered at 5.112-5.157 Angstrom
#   (mean 5.132 A), well separated from the next shell (mixed same/opposite-sublattice,
#   starting 5.411 A) -- clean single-shell cutoff.
#   For H = -sum J'_ij (unit-vector si.sj), per-formula-unit energy bookkeeping gives
#     dE_total = z * J'_eff  =>  J'_eff = dE / z = 0.04823354 / 4 = 0.012058 eV = 12.06 meV
#   This treats the whole shell as one effective bond (mean-field-style single-J fit) --
#   the same level of approximation as the "effective nearest-neighbor" pdfeir model, not a
#   full multi-shell J(r) fit. FM being the DFT ground state (dE>0) is correctly reproduced
#   by a positive J' (favors alignment).
#
#   mu_s = 4.15 mu_B, averaged from OUTCAR magnetization (Fe tot moment 4.158-4.162 in FM,
#   4.134-4.140 in AFM).
#
# --- DMI: DFT-derived (paramrudra jobs 49186/49187, data/dft_staging_noncollinear/mp-754090/).
#   Method: two constrained noncollinear+SOC static calcs, Fe0 fixed along +z, Fe1 constrained
#   to +x (canted_plus) and -x (canted_minus) -- i.e. theta=+-90deg canting in the xz-plane.
#   Constraint held cleanly (OUTCAR per-ion magnetization: Fe1 = 4.038/-4.039 ucB along x in
#   the two jobs, Fe0 leakage off z < 0.002 ucB). Using E(theta) = E0 - z*J*cos(theta) -
#   z*D*sin(theta) with z=4 (same coordination shell as the J fit) and free energy TOTEN
#   (same convention as the J derivation, for consistency):
#     F(canted_plus)  = -126.06989762 eV  (Fe1 -> +x)
#     F(canted_minus) = -126.06835168 eV  (Fe1 -> -x)
#     z*D = [F(canted_minus) - F(canted_plus)] / 2 = 0.77297 meV  =>  D = 0.19324 meV
#   Since S1=z and the canting is in the xz-plane, S1 x S2 = (0, sin(theta), 0) -- this probe
#   measures D_y specifically (the DMI vector's y-component in this lab frame), not a generic
#   magnitude. D/J ~ 1.6%, notably smaller than the earlier placeholder guess (~25% of J).
#   Caveat: mp-754090 has no symmetry (space group P1, see dmi_setup_notes.md) to fix which
#   plane the *true* DMI vector lives in -- x was an arbitrary but fixed reference axis, so
#   this D is a real DFT number for the probed plane, not a fully resolved 3D DMI vector.
#   Anisotropy and any other DMI components remain unprobed.
#
# --- Anisotropy: unknown, set to 0 (no single-ion anisotropy term). Not guessed -- no DFT
#   or literature basis for a value or easy-axis direction for this compound.
#
# Known LAMMPS build issues (same machine/build as pdfeir, see in.pdfeir_dynamics.lammps):
#   hybrid/overlay segfaults with exactly 2 spin substyles; padded to 3 with a zero-strength
#   spin/magelec substyle as a workaround, not a physics change.

units           metal
atom_style      spin
dimension       3
boundary        p p p
atom_modify     map array

# Real triclinic cell (Angstrom, from mp-754090 POSCAR), 2-atom Fe-only basis.
#
# NOTE: an earlier version of this file used `lattice custom` (non-orthogonal a1/a2/a3) +
# `region prism ... 0 0 0 units lattice`, assuming zero tilt in lattice units would inherit
# the custom lattice's own skew. Smoke test proved this WRONG (no crash, no NaN -- silently
# wrong instead): LAMMPS built an orthogonal box (reported tilt "(0 0 0)" literally, i.e. no
# skew applied) with a fabricated "lattice spacing" that matched none of a1/a2/a3, giving 136
# atoms instead of the expected 24 for a 3x2x2 replication. Fixed by instead writing an
# explicit triclinic data file (mp754090_fe.data, lower-triangular convention, tilt
# hand-derived from a1/a2/a3 via a1hat/xy/ly/xz/yz -- volume-checked against
# det(a1,a2,a3)=206.827 before trusting it) and using read_data + replicate, which handles
# triclinic geometry correctly. Re-verified: this version gives exactly nx*ny*nz*2 atoms.
read_data       mp754090_fe.data
variable        nx equal 16
variable        ny equal 8
variable        nz equal 8
replicate       ${nx} ${ny} ${nz}

set             group all spin/atom/random 31 4.15   # mu_s = 4.15 mu_B, random init (paramagnetic start)

# --- Exchange: J_eff = 12.058 meV = 0.012058 eV, Bethe-Slater fit, single-shell cutoff ---
variable        j_eff_eV equal 0.012058385
variable        d_shell equal 5.132075
variable        exch_a equal v_j_eff_eV*2.718281828/4.0
variable        rc_exch equal 5.25          # includes z=4 shell (5.112-5.157 A), excludes next (5.411 A)

# --- DMI: DFT-derived, |D| = 0.19324 meV, direction y -- see note above ---
variable        d_eV equal 0.00019324
variable        rc_dmi equal 5.25

pair_style      hybrid/overlay spin/exchange ${rc_exch} spin/dmi ${rc_dmi} spin/magelec ${rc_exch}
pair_coeff      * * spin/exchange exchange ${rc_exch} ${exch_a} 0.0 ${d_shell} offset yes
pair_coeff      * * spin/dmi dmi ${rc_dmi} ${d_eV} 0.0 1.0 0.0
pair_coeff      * * spin/magelec magelec ${rc_exch} 0.0 1.0 1.0 1.0   # zero strength: segfault workaround only

neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    every 10 check yes delay 20

fix             1 all precession/spin zeeman 0.0 0.0 0.0 1.0
fix_modify      1 energy yes
fix             2 all langevin/spin 0.0 0.05 21      # damping placeholder, matches pdfeir convention
fix             3 all nve/spin lattice frozen         # rigid lattice, spin-only dynamics

timestep        0.0001

compute         outsp all property/atom spx spy spz sp
dump            1 all custom 500 dump_mp754090_T0.lammpstrj type x y z c_outsp[1] c_outsp[2] c_outsp[3]

thermo_style    custom step pe etotal
thermo          200

min_style       spin/lbfgs
minimize        1.0e-10 1.0e-12 5000 10000

write_restart   restart.mp754090_T0.equil
